================================================================================
2. WHAT THIS SOFTWARE DOES
================================================================================

Read this section before installing or running the Software. It is networking
and cryptographic software, and by design it:

  * installs and operates a VIRTUAL NETWORK ADAPTER on the host system, which
    requires ADMINISTRATOR / ELEVATED PRIVILEGES to create;
  * performs NAT TRAVERSAL ("hole punching"), deliberately opening a path
    through network address translators that may not match assumptions made
    by firewalls or other network controls;
  * ENCRYPTS traffic between Peers, making that traffic opaque to network
    operators, monitoring tools, and inspection systems on the path;
  * CARRIES ARBITRARY IP TRAFFIC — including broadcast and multicast, where
    enabled — between connected machines, making a Peer's machine appear as
    though it were on your local network, and vice versa.

Connecting to a Peer extends your network boundary to include that Peer, and
anything reachable through them. Misconfiguration or misuse can create
security risk not only for you but for third parties, and for any network you
or your Peer are attached to. You are responsible for understanding this
before you use the Software.

